type: software
title: "Meshtastic Logistics Metadata Collector: Open-Source Software for Measuring the Operational Autonomy of SME Logistics over LoRa Mesh Networks"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-28
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Prokopovych-Tkachenko"
    given-names: "Dmytro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6590-3898"
    affiliation: "Department of Cybersecurity and Information Technologies, University of Customs and Finance, Dnipro, Ukraine"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23796017
    description: "Version 1.0.0. The DOI of version 1.1.0 is assigned by Zenodo at deposit."
abstract: >-
  Python software for a private Meshtastic LoRa mesh network used as a backup channel for critical
  logistics operations of small and medium-sized enterprises. A gateway collector records packet,
  device and logistics-event metadata into a local SQLite store; a 24-byte binary protocol on
  PRIVATE_APP (port 256) carries EVENT/ACCEPT/DONE messages; kpi.py computes the field counterparts
  of the quantities predicted by the accompanying article (channel utilisation, delivery ratio, age
  of information, on-time completion, operational autonomy) with provenance, sample sizes and
  intervals. Evidence status: exercised only on an invented replay log; never run on radio
  hardware; no output of this package is a measurement.
keywords:
  - Meshtastic
  - LoRa
  - mesh network
  - SME logistics
  - supply chain resilience
  - business continuity
  - operational autonomy
  - age of information
  - metadata collection
  - SQLite
